IV. Internal Logic of the Sequence
4.1 Conceptual Gradation
The six-fold sequence reflects a logical progression:
1.	Foundational: From "What do I see?" to "How do I see?"
2.	Developmental: From "How do I see?" to "How do I live time?"
3.	Meta-Critical: From "How do I critique the Other?" to "How do I critique myself?"
4.	Universal-Experimental: From "How do I understand?" to "How much can I endure?"
5.	Post-Universal: From "What follows collapse?" to "Can we rebuild?"
6.	Ritual-Universal: From "How do I perceive?" to "What is the meaning of existence?"
4.2 Architectural Structure
The movement can be likened to an integrated architectural structure:
•	Ritual-Universal: (The Dome – Spiritual Contemplation)
•	Post-Universal: (The Roof – Post-Collapse)
•	Universal-Experimental: (The Pillars – Endurance Testing)
•	Meta-Critical: (The Mirror – Self-Critique)
•	Developmental: (The Walls – Experiencing Time)
•	Foundational: (The Foundation – Deconstructing Perception)
________________________________________
V. Conclusion
The six-fold classification of the "Post-Perception" movement represents a holistic methodological framework. This structure is not merely a sorting tool; it is a reflection of the movement's philosophical vision: perception is an evolving process that begins with sensory skepticism and passes through time-experience, self-critique, and the questioning of existence, reaching a final contemplation of meaning.
A living movement is never complete. This classification remains open to additional categories and works as the movement evolves.
